    "scope": "8.h.W adds compare_semantic over explicit ComparisonInputs. Every supplied stored artifact field contract is validated before classification. Existing artifact identities, hashes, presence flags, values and pointers remain visible. Threshold/text, scope/exception/relation/document/verification/code-reference differences retain their structural classes; applicability, product configuration, stored statuses and evidence result/binding/content changes are distinguished. Paired typed ProjectConfigurations compare through the existing semantic projection and also bind their raw declarations. Explicit requirement timing bounds alone enable exact tightened/relaxed/equivalent/incomparable duration observations; policies bind even unchanged input. Missing configuration is not_supplied. Supplied inventory membership deltas do not imply applicability-derived scope, which remains not_evaluated alongside evidence currency. Independent tests cover classes, exact values/identities, configuration and policy binding, invalid inputs, ownership, no writes and fresh-process parity. Existing 277 test files and 9227 IDs remain unchanged. Source adapters, Diff CLI, durable Work, effective profiles, applicability-derived scope, evidence-currentness services and platform/performance acceptance remain open; no release approval is claimed. R classifies additional unstructured domain text and text-bearing namespaced extension values as text_changed without interpreting words, languages, Markdown or numerical claims. Opaque extension keys never inherit Core timing/threshold/status/evidence semantics. Pure numeric/Boolean unknown deltas remain structural field_changed; declared enum, identity and path values keep their existing classes. Iterative value scanning retains complete containers, presence/null distinctions, escaped pointers and exact Unicode bytes. Independent tests cover twenty domain/record text positions, misleading extension names, typed machine values, deep/wide data, ownership, ordering and read-only boundaries. All 278 old test files and 9263 IDs remain unchanged; all W cases remain part of selected regression. Source/CLI/Work integration, effective profiles, evaluated scope/currency and platform/performance acceptance remain open. C moves all declared-field, opaque-text, paired-configuration and explicit-duration classifiers into a private module. All five extracted definitions and the public comparison function retain identical source and AST; only module ownership and necessary imports change. All 279 old test files and 9310 IDs remain unchanged. Existing W/R behavior is rerun through the public API; no new semantic classes, error contracts, side effects or authority are introduced. Later providers and acceptance remain open. 9.h.W evaluates explicitly paired stored configuration IDs in the existing semantic comparison and source adapters. Parent/value/applicability changes retain their semantic classes; actual applicable ID sets yield exact added/removed/retained scope membership, distinct from the stored inventory delta. Effective manifests and complete stored dependency evaluations bind the result input hash. Native Diff --configuration selects the same ID in both actual snapshots, preserves full paths and returns complete model failure SRV131 if either variant is inconsistent. Missing or invalid selection produces SRV130 without a partial result. Unselected comparison remains byte-equivalent in data semantics, with configuration scope not_evaluated. New tests cover actual side deltas, parent switching, selection-only changes, owned values, source/CLI/request/Work parity, late source changes, no writes and portable execution. External resource closure, evidence currency, Merge and configuration-bound Baselines remain separate unavailable providers. 9.h.R rebuilds configured ComparisonInputs from original SourceRelations bytes before any general field/inventory comparison; cached caller identities cannot diverge from the separately evaluated configuration. New reference cases cover nested defaults and overrides, invalid inherited values and cycles on both sides, inconsistent-before/fixed-after and both-side dependency paths with deterministic shortest ties, local/Git source/CLI/Work parity, pinned Git refs, late changes to either snapshot, concurrency and no writes. Existing W tests remain unchanged. Configuration-bound Baselines and complete resource/evidence providers remain open. 9.h.C places the unchanged variant-scope and owned configured-input functions in the existing private semantic classifier module. Both extracted function sources/AST and the public comparison function remain identical; existing classifiers and all test files remain byte-identical. Only module ownership and required imports change. The same W/R behavior is rerun against this separate C state. No new semantic classes, errors, side effects, Baseline provider or approval is introduced."
